{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals","id":684528,"title":"Hot Button Political Issues for Sidereals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-01T09:23:20-07:00","id":684528,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Hot Button Political Issues for Sidereals","content":"(This is a spin off thread from the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/677864-there-are-only-100-sidereals-so-how-are-there-so-many-factions\">There are only 100 sidereals...so how are there so many factions?</a> topic.)<br /> <br /> The Great Prophecy is over a thousand years old and the majority of Sidereals were not even alive when it was cast. With the return of the Solars happening only in the last year, there must have been other Political Issues for Sidereals to argue about over the past thousand years. Right now, there is the perception that Sidereal political beliefs are basically &quot;Do you like Solars? Yes or No.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would like to start brain storming other Political Issues to for Sidereals to be divided over. There can still be a Gold and a Bronze Faction, but like Political Parties in the US, the Faction evolve with leadership supplying direction on key issues. Of course that doesn't mean that every Sidereal in the faction agrees with Faction leadership. I think having a diverse set of issues would lead to more back room dealings between Factions and less &quot;Kill Sidereals that don't agree with me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here is a start of my list. Feel Free to add your own.<br /> <br /> 1. Do you support the Scarlet Empress and the Realm?<br /> 2. Do you believe that all &quot;Lost Eggs&quot; should be recruited by the Realm?<br /> 3. Should other non-Realm groups of Dragonblooded, such as the Seventh Legion, be allowed to exist?<br /> 3. How much should Dragonblooded know about First Age History?<br /> 4. Should Dangerous First Age Artifacts be allowed to Dragonblooded?<br /> 5. Should Sidereals concern themselves with raising the standard of living in Creation?<br /> 6. Should effort be made to maintain failing First Age Infrastructure in the Threshold?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-01-2015, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:36:04-07:00","id":684560,"title":"","content":"Should the Sidereals encourage or discourage Lookshy's (a Dragonblood, anti-Anathema country) resistance to the Realm?<br /> <br /> How important is it for the Immaculate Order to encourage genuinely moral behaviour, or should they just focus on maintaining Realm control?<br /> <br /> Should Ronin be forcibly returned to Yu-Shan to do their jobs?<br /> On a more extreme position, should Ronin be executed for desertion, so their exaltation can reincarnate into someone who does their job?<br /> <br /> How much resources should the Five-Score Fellowship spend clamping down on demon cults, when the Yozis are imprisoned?<br /> <br /> Is it okay for a pre-Sidereal to do jobs that a Sidereal is supposed to do?<br /> <br /> Again, if the Yozis are imprisoned, how much can Sidereals use bound demons (in terms of the confidentiality of a Sidereal's job)?<br /> <br /> Should Sidereals be subject to divine censure?<br /> <br /> How should Sidereals act vis-\u00e0-vis divine corruption? Is it any of their business?<br /> <br /> What is the best kind of tea in Creation?<br /> <br /> Do you believe that Eyes-of-Moonlight, the Chosen of Serenity who was executed for grand treason and infernalism in 598RY, really was an Akuma, or did Anys Syn frame him for asking the wrong questions?<br /> <br /> Do you believe that Shajah Holok should be prosecuted for his involvement in the Ten Clan Mountain massacre?<br /> <br /> Should the Sidereals destroy the shrines on the Caul so as to get the Dragonblood to stop wasting lives and resources there?<br /> <br /> These are all fairly minor ones. Here's the big one:<br /> <br /> Who should be the new Emperor/Empress of the Realm?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:37:27-07:00","id":684562,"title":"","content":"7. How much should we use Necromancy against the Death Lords?<br /> 8. How should we deal with Abyssals/Death Knights?<br /> 9. should we negotiate with the Lunars more?<br /> 10. Assuming we do like Solars, how are we going to handle them so that they don't screw everything up again?<br /> 11. Should we come clean about the Usurpation?<br /> 12. How far should we use demons?<br /> 13. Should we try to expand the Loom of Fate to cover Malfeas and the Underworld as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:48:06-07:00","id":684569,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I quibble somewhat with this list, W&amp;A.<br /> <br /> One is going to be a salient issue for a lot of Sidereals, although prior to the return of the Solars it will likely be more a theoretical exercise than anything.<br /> <br /> Two is something that I don't think even the Bronze Faction is going to care about. What is it to the Sidereals if random Outcaste Dragon-Blooded joins up with the Realm or not? I mean... why would they care enough one way or the other to devote resources to it, and even if you don't like the Realm, do you not like it enough to track down random outcastes and try to ensure they don't go to the Realm?<br /> <br /> Three is tricky. Lookshy is actually protected by the Maidens themselves (Mars specifically, I think) from too much meddling. There really aren't significant non-Realm organizations of the Dragon-Blooded besides them. It's like... ooo, the Forest Witches. If they end up on the Sidereals radar it will be for official reasons, not for unofficial faction business.<br /> <br /> Other three is going to be resolutely answered &quot;the official Immaculate version of history of the First Age, the one we wrote, is what they should know.&quot; Even if you disagree with that line, how are you going to undermine the massive edifice of seven hundred years of propaganda, supported by both powerful faction elders and the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> Four is going to be something that the Scarlet Empress, who operates the most potent First Age Artifact of them all, has an opinion on. If you're Bronze, you probably give that opinion great weight. If you're not, the answer is likely &quot;none of this stuff can be trusted to the Dragon-Blooded or the Lunars, it should be in our hands.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hell, even if you're Bronze, you probably share that opinion, you just don't share it enough to outright steal shit from the Realm without treading lightly.<br /> <br /> Five, Sidereals definitely concern themselves with the standard of living in Creation, but they have so many other things to do that it may just be something they don't gots time for. Theoretically, the other Exalted are meant to worry about things like that.<br /> <br /> Six is going to be dependent on how much that infrastructure ties into their jobs. They probably don't give a shit about rich people in Chiaroscuro having magical streetlights. They probably give a lot of shits about making sure the Lap doesn't catastrophically fail one day and ignite half the dragon lines across the whole direction.<br /> <br /> Really, a lot of these are issues the Sidereals are not going to consider huge priorities prior to the return of the Solars, even people who are heavily into faction stuff. I have trouble seeing a lot of it causing huge divides on its own.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:56:40-07:00","id":684581,"title":"","content":"28. Is Arcane Fate actually necessary anymore? Is it more hinderance than help? Should we try to repair the Mask?<br /> <br /> 29. Should we continue to focus on fighting Lunars, or try to focus more on the Deathlords?<br /> <br /> 30. Should we allow the Lunars to maintain &quot;buffer states&quot; in the outer Threshold to help hold back the Fae, or continue wiping them out?<br /> <br /> 31. Should Sidereal children still be allowed to grow up in Creation, or should we take them all to Yu-Shan for their safety and/or indoctrination?<br /> <br /> 32. How much should Sidereal children be told of the truth before they Exalt?<br /> <br /> 33. How much should they be told after they exalt? Are there things the younger Sidereals just should not know?<br /> <br /> 34. Should we continue to treat Lunars and Solars the same? Should we try to negotiate with Lunars while still killing Solars? Or try to reform and restore the Solars but keep killing Lunars?<br /> <br /> 35. Should we interfere with the Elemental war? Is the disruption the Air Elementals are causing/the disruption Water Elementals could cause a problem for fate?<br /> <br /> 36. Should we try to gain more influence over the Aerial Legion and if so, how?<br /> <br /> 37. Probably lots of disagreements about specific relations with specific other Bureaus... that I know nothing about.<br /> <br /> 38. Something about how to handle Exigents... again I know nothing about it.<br /> <br /> 39. Should the Realm be the only Dragon-Blooded power in Creation? Should Sidereals actively encourage/build/manipulate others? Is the Realm even a good way for Dragon-Bloods to be organized?<br /> <br /> 40. Is it really a good idea to discourage Dragon-Blooded population growth? (This seems related to the Realm grabbing all the Lost Eggs.)<br /> <br /> 41. What are we going to do about the Deathlords?<br /> <br /> 42. How are we going to find out what caused the Great Contagion so we can prevent another one?<br /> <br /> 43. How much corruption among Sidereals is acceptable while persuing missions? To what extent should Sidereals be held responsible for grotesque corruption, and by whom?<br /> <br /> 44. Are the presence of shadowlands and Wyld zones in Creation a threat to the integrity of the world or to fate? Should we do anything to repair them?<br /> <br /> 45. Should we keep suppressing that one Dragon King Path (can't remember which one they're suppressing).<br /> <br /> 46. Should we try to revive the Dragon Kings somewhat and encourage/manipulate them to oppose enemies of Creation?<br /> <br /> 47. What is going on with Stygia and how much should we try to meddle in... whatever is going on down there?<br /> <br /> 48. (Gold Faction) Should we teach Sidereal Martial Arts to Solars? Encourage them to or prevent them from recovering Solar Circle Sorcery?<br /> <br /> 49. (Bronze Faction?) Should Anys Syn keep exploding elite Dragon-Bloods in her quest for ultimate kung-fu?<br /> <br /> 50. The Guild. A vehicle for suffering (slavery, war) and allies of the Fair Folk that should be reformed or even dismantled? A vital trade-network that keeps humanity alive, keeps Creation shaped, and should be protected or even strengthened? A threat to Sidereals whose missions conflict with Guild profit? Can/should it be used to restore the Order-Conferring Trade Pattern to its former strength? If we did go so far as to dismantle it what would replace it?<br /> <br /> 51. What is the best way to police our own ranks for akuma?<br /> <br /> 52. Is there any threat big enough that we could work together with Lunars to stop it? How big? How many Lunars?<br /> <br /> 53. Does creating or encouraging schools of thaumaturgy, Terrestrial Martial Arts, or Sorcery among mortals threaten fate, or could it be a tool to help humans or oppose enemies of Creation? If so how should we go about doing that?<br /> <br /> 54. How much occult knowledge should mortals have? How much is enough to know how to avoid the most common demon/fae/ghost tricks, demon escapes, etc.? How much is too much (enough to start doing dangerous shit)?<br /> <br /> 55. (Bronze) Should we try to pry the Emerald Thurible out of Mnemon's hands?<br /> <br /> 56. How much time and effort and money should we spend trying to stamp out necromancy and hungry ghost creation among mortals?<br /> <br /> 57. How much time and effort and money should we spend trying to stamp out ancestor worship among mortals?<br /> <br /> 58. Can we use the Mountain Folk more... usefully? They don't exactly have mountains of starmetal but they can do and make cool stuff.<br /> <br /> 59. Bureau of Humanity vs. Bureau of Destiny dispute who has more jurisdiction over warfare. How important is this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-01-2015, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T15:10:04-07:00","id":684939,"title":"","content":"I feel like Sidereals should argue (or at least debate and discuss) the meanings of the Scriptures of the Maidens more actively. I mean, these are (presumably) the divine words of their patron goddesses! There should be groups of Journeys who try to figure out what is meant by &quot;I have no use for beginnings&quot; in the Scripture of the Eternal Maiden, and cliques who try to discern the meaning of the incredibly arcane Scripture of Absence. <br /> <br /> Remember that Sidereals aren't <i>just</i> overworked Heavenly bureaucrat fate ninjas - they're also Chosen by the Maidens, and anything the Maidens say should be treated with reverence, or at least a deep respect. The Maidens aren't just the Sidereals' superiors, they're their <i>goddesses</i>, and I think that gets forgotten a lot because the Sidereals work with other gods and goddesses. I still hold, however, that the Sidereals are probably amongst the more devout of the Exalt types, by simple virtue of proximity - the Maidens are just close enough to impress you with their divine nature and overpowering presence, while remaining distant and enigmatic enough that you can still revere them easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T15:31:21-07:00","id":684962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=684939#post684939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Sidereals should argue (or at least debate and discuss) the meanings of the Scriptures of the Maidens more actively. I mean, these are (presumably) the divine words of their <b>patron</b> goddesses! There should be groups of Journeys who try to figure out what is meant by &quot;I have no use for beginnings&quot; in the Scripture of the Eternal Maiden, and cliques who try to discern the meaning of the incredibly arcane Scripture of Absence.<br /> <br /> Remember that Sidereals aren't <i>just</i> overworked Heavenly bureaucrat fate ninjas - they're also Chosen by the Maidens, and anything the Maidens say should be treated with reverence, or at least a deep respect. The Maidens aren't just the Sidereals' superiors, they're their <i>goddesses</i>, and I think that gets forgotten a lot because the Sidereals work with other gods and goddesses. I still hold, however, that the Sidereals are probably amongst the more devout of the Exalt types, by simple virtue of proximity - the Maidens are just close enough to impress you with their divine nature and overpowering presence, while remaining distant and enigmatic enough that you can still revere them easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matron.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree. In general, I'd like more focus on religion and philosophy in Creation. The Sidereals are particularly interesting, as their gods are actually literally their bosses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T15:45:35-07:00","id":684986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=684939#post684939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Sidereals should argue (or at least debate and discuss) the meanings of the Scriptures of the Maidens more actively. I mean, these are (presumably) the divine words of their patron goddesses! There should be groups of Journeys who try to figure out what is meant by &quot;I have no use for beginnings&quot; in the Scripture of the Eternal Maiden, and cliques who try to discern the meaning of the incredibly arcane Scripture of Absence.<br /> <br /> Remember that Sidereals aren't <i>just</i> overworked Heavenly bureaucrat fate ninjas - they're also Chosen by the Maidens, and anything the Maidens say should be treated with reverence, or at least a deep respect. The Maidens aren't just the Sidereals' superiors, they're their <i>goddesses</i>, and I think that gets forgotten a lot because the Sidereals work with other gods and goddesses. I still hold, however, that the Sidereals are probably amongst the more devout of the Exalt types, by simple virtue of proximity - the Maidens are just close enough to impress you with their divine nature and overpowering presence, while remaining distant and enigmatic enough that you can still revere them easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the scriptures were <b>adopted</b> by the individual Maidens according to preference - Sidereals 1e made it clear that someone left them entangled into the Loom itself from where they were taken by the Maidens for their own reasons and made charms from. If it was Jupiter or someone else altogether that left the scriptures there in the first place is in itself pretty much a mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T18:23:43-07:00","id":685119,"title":"","content":"Well now that's interesting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T19:30:00-07:00","id":685150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=685119#post685119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well now that's interesting!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also something that gets a call-out in Infernals with One-Hand Fury and the Scripture of the One-Handed Maiden, in fact.<br /> <br /> That said, the power of the Yozis being connected to the Scriptures doesn't mean they got one up on the Maidens or the Sidereals - it could just as well reflect the Loom dredging up cosmic truths inadvertently infused in the weft of Creation itself. Or that some powerful but mysterious entity stole secrets from the Titans themselves Prometheus-style and wove them into the Loom for the Maidens to find, among other potential alternatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T20:32:35-07:00","id":685174,"title":"","content":"Fools! Now I shall ANSWER these questions!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>1. Do you support the Scarlet Empress and the Realm?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, literally- I spend a great deal of time standing behind the Scarlet Throne simply because the back broke off four centuries ago and if you lean on it too hard it falls over.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Do you believe that all &quot;Lost Eggs&quot; should be recruited by the Realm?</b><br /> <br /> Of course! Or are you suggesting that there's a problem with poached Eggs?<br /> <br /> <b>3. Should other non-Realm groups of Dragonblooded, such as the Seventh Legion, be allowed to exist?</b><br /> <br /> Technically speaking, the Seventh Legion is still part of the Realm. It's just a... very entrenched splinter group.<br /> <br /> <b>3. How much should Dragonblooded know about First Age History?</b><br /> <br /> I'm not sure this is a meaningful question- all records of civilization that long ago are going to be biased in some way. The fact that the Realm has a very usefully biased history is of small moment.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Should Dangerous First Age Artifacts be allowed to Dragonblooded?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, but only if they can first solve my fiendish maze.<br /> <br /> <b>5. Should Sidereals concern themselves with raising the standard of living in Creation?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, but they can focus on the mean rather than the median.<br /> <br /> <b>6. Should effort be made to maintain failing First Age Infrastructure in the Threshold?</b><br /> <br /> This really depends on whether we're talking about the Puppy-Petting Manse of Ultimate Happiness or Bright Shattered Ice's Ultramurder Ray.<br /> <br /> <b>7. How much should we use Necromancy against the Death Lords?</b><br /> <br /> Twelve.<br /> <br /> <b>8. How should we deal with Abyssals/Death Knights?</b><br /> <br /> Under UCC principles as opposed to the common law of contracts.<br /> <br /> <b>9. should we negotiate with the Lunars more?</b><br /> <br /> No, they're just playing hardball. We go back to the table now, they'll demand fifteen percent increases to the last letter of intent. I say we tell 'em that it's our way or the fathomless chaos beyond Time.<br /> <br /> <b>10. Assuming we do like Solars, how are we going to handle them so that they don't screw everything up again?</b><br /> <br /> We could try stacking three or four Sidereals in a suit and pretending they're just one really tall guy in order to intimidate them.<br /> <br /> <b>11. Should we come clean about the Usurpation?</b><br /> <br /> Let's wait until Hallmark releases an appropriate apology card. That way we don't look cheap.<br /> <br /> <b>12. How far should we use demons?</b><br /> <br /> Typically about three days' travel through an endless desert.<br /> <br /> <b>13. Should we try to expand the Loom of Fate to cover Malfeas and the Underworld as well?</b><br /> <br /> NO.<br /> <br /> <b>14. Should the Sidereals encourage or discourage Lookshy's (a Dragonblood, anti-Anathema country) resistance to the Realm?</b><br /> <br /> Let's denounce it in public but secretly donate to their SuperPAC.<br /> <br /> <b>15. How important is it for the Immaculate Order to encourage genuinely moral behaviour, or should they just focus on maintaining Realm control?</b><br /> <br /> Oh god, don't open up ethical questions again or Aquillion will be in here with more trolley problem charms.<br /> <br /> <b>16. Should Ronin be forcibly returned to Yu-Shan to do their jobs? </b><b>On a more extreme position, should Ronin be executed for desertion, so their exaltation can reincarnate into someone who does their job?</b><br /> <br /> My answer to this depends a lot on how far you can abuse your annual leave before you're marked 'Ronin'.<br /> <br /> <b>17. How much resources should the Five-Score Fellowship spend clamping down on demon cults, when the Yozis are imprisoned?</b><br /> <br /> Probably about Resources 4?<br /> <br /> <b>18. Is it okay for a pre-Sidereal to do jobs that a Sidereal is supposed to do?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, but they don't get worker's comp.<br /> <br /> <b>19. Again, if the Yozis are imprisoned, how much can Sidereals use bound demons (in terms of the confidentiality of a Sidereal's job)?</b><br /> <br /> Employees are encouraged to use divine prostitutes rather than infernal ones, in order to encourage a vibrant local economy.<br /> <br /> <b>20. Should Sidereals be subject to divine censure?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, but they should get commuted sentences if they quote verbatim the famous courtroom blockbuster from 'And Justice For All'<br /> <br /> <b>21. How should Sidereals act vis-\u00e0-vis divine corruption? Is it any of their business?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, under the holding in <u>James v. United States</u>, 366 U.S. 213 (1961).<br /> <br /> <b>22. What is the best kind of tea in Creation?</b><br /> <br /> It's a special leaf which grows exclusively in my Unreachable Gardens.<br /> <br /> <b>23. Do you believe that Eyes-of-Moonlight, the Chosen of Serenity who was executed for grand treason and infernalism in 598RY, really was an Akuma, or did Anys Syn frame him for asking the wrong questions?</b><br /> <br /> Wow, people really buy these conspiracy theories? Anys Syn is a model citizen who would never lie about infernalism or bribe Bureau executives with enormous sums of money.<br /> <br /> <b>24. Do you believe that Shajah Holok should be prosecuted for his involvement in the Ten Clan Mountain massacre?</b><br /> <br /> No. I do not believe that mountains have human rights, nor do I recognize the validity of foreign court decisions which compel such a result.<br /> <br /> <b>25. Should the Sidereals destroy the shrines on the Caul so as to get the Dragonblood to stop wasting lives and resources there?</b><br /> <br /> No- they'd just waste those lives and resources somewhere else.<br /> <br /> <b>26. These are all fairly minor ones. Here's the big one:</b><br /> <br /> Oh snap.<br /> <br /> <b>27. Who should be the new Emperor/Empress of the Realm?</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/John_Cena_134616.jpg/800px-John_Cena_134616.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>28. Is Arcane Fate actually necessary anymore? Is it more hinderance than help? Should we try to repair the Mask?</b><br /> <br /> No, you'd just make it look all lopsided.<br /> <br /> <b>29. Should we continue to focus on fighting Lunars, or try to focus more on the Deathlords?</b><br /> <br /> These 'deathlords' are an obvious ploy by the Lunar resistance to try to end what must be a highly-successful initiative on our part. Now is the time to redouble our efforts and ignore false flag operations..<br /> <br /> <b>30. Should we allow the Lunars to maintain &quot;buffer states&quot; in the outer Threshold to help hold back the Fae, or continue wiping them out?</b><br /> <br /> Absolutely not- buffering is just the first step towards loading and fully playing their flash video of despair.<br /> <br /> <b>31. Should Sidereal children still be allowed to grow up in Creation, or should we take them all to Yu-Shan for their safety and/or indoctrination?</b><br /> <br /> I say that we use Pattern Spider Touch to install those children as rulers of various Threshold states for a term of years in order to ensure a thorough education.<br /> <br /> <b>32. How much should Sidereal children be told of the truth before they Exalt?</b><br /> <br /> Nothing. In fact, I'm pushing for regulations which would require that all Sidereal children be exclusively told outrageous lies for my personal entertainment.<br /> <br /> <b>33. How much should they be told after they exalt? Are there things the younger Sidereals just should not know?</b><br /> <br /> Well, we probably should keep a lid on the <i>Word Which Causes Instant Death If You Know It</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>34. Should we continue to treat Lunars and Solars the same? Should we try to negotiate with Lunars while still killing Solars? Or try to reform and restore the Solars but keep killing Lunars?</b><br /> <br /> We should split the Lunar and Solar populations in half and attempt to negotiate with one of the halves while slaughtering the other so that we maintain a control group and can get this experiment published in good journals.<br /> <br /> <b>35. Should we interfere with the Elemental war? Is the disruption the Air Elementals are causing/the disruption Water Elementals could cause a problem for fate?</b><br /> <br /> All the fog makes the Loom soggy and the Pattern Spiders run into each other.<br /> <br /> <b>36. Should we try to gain more influence over the Aerial Legion and if so, how?</b><br /> <br /> I'm trying to get a Sidereal installed as Air Traffic Controller, so that if a Solar ever calls upon the Aerial Legion they won't be able to take off.<br /> <br /> <b>37. Probably lots of disagreements about specific relations with specific other Bureaus... that I know nothing about.</b><br /> <br /> FUCK YOU O-TOLKANO, SHOGUN OF LINGUISTIC DRIFT.<br /> <br /> <b>38. Something about how to handle Exigents... again I know nothing about it.</b><br /> <br /> I say we build a terrifying bleak fortress in the far north and lock them up in it.<br /> <br /> <b>39. Should the Realm be the only Dragon-Blooded power in Creation? Should Sidereals actively encourage/build/manipulate others? Is the Realm even a good way for Dragon-Bloods to be organized?</b><br /> <br /> Don't look at me- I pushed for a constitutional oligarchy, but apparently a cannon the size of a continent means more than traditional voting processes.<br /> <br /> <b>40. Is it really a good idea to discourage Dragon-Blooded population growth? (This seems related to the Realm grabbing all the Lost Eggs.)</b><br /> <br /> This sounds like yet another problem which could be easily addressed through wild orgies.<br /> <br /> <b>41. What are we going to do about the Deathlords?</b><br /> <br /> Don't you worry- I've put them all on Do Not Hire lists, and if anyone calls I'm going to give them dreadful references.<br /> <br /> <b>42. How are we going to find out what caused the Great Contagion so we can prevent another one?</b><br /> <br /> At this point in time we're about 98% sure it was foul odors and humors, so we're issuing gigantic beak-shaped masks full of smelling salts to everyone.<br /> <br /> <b>43. How much corruption among Sidereals is acceptable while persuing missions? To what extent should Sidereals be held responsible for grotesque corruption, and by whom?</b><br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'm a fan of this new trend of ascribing aesthetic sensibilities to corruption.<br /> <br /> <b>44. Are the presence of shadowlands and Wyld zones in Creation a threat to the integrity of the world or to fate? Should we do anything to repair them?</b><br /> <br /> Don't scratch them!<br /> <br /> <b>45. Should we keep suppressing that one Dragon King Path (can't remember which one they're suppressing).</b><br /> <br /> This is not a big issue- Dragon King Paths sort of start out pre-suppressed.<br /> <br /> <b>46. Should we try to revive the Dragon Kings somewhat and encourage/manipulate them to oppose enemies of Creation?</b><br /> <br /> Where the hell do you think we're going to find the budget for that?<br /> <br /> <b>47. What is going on with Stygia and how much should we try to meddle in... whatever is going on down there?</b><br /> <br /> It's probably just a phase.<br /> <br /> <b>48. (Gold Faction) Should we teach Sidereal Martial Arts to Solars? Encourage them to or prevent them from recovering Solar Circle Sorcery?</b><br /> <br /> You can't teach Solars SMA- I hold a copyright to all of the styles. They'll need to apply with me for an exception.<br /> <br /> <b>49. (Bronze Faction?) Should Anys Syn keep exploding elite Dragon-Bloods in her quest for ultimate kung-fu?</b><br /> <br /> Look, she doesn't complain about YOUR hobbies.<br /> <br /> <b>50. The Guild. A vehicle for suffering (slavery, war) and allies of the Fair Folk that should be reformed or even dismantled? A vital trade-network that keeps humanity alive, keeps Creation shaped, and should be protected or even strengthened? A threat to Sidereals whose missions conflict with Guild profit? Can/should it be used to restore the Order-Conferring Trade Pattern to its former strength? If we did go so far as to dismantle it what would replace it?</b><br /> <br /> Amazon Prime.<br /> <br /> <b>51. What is the best way to police our own ranks for akuma?</b><br /> <br /> I'm thinking a poster campaign. 'Winners don't sacrifice their souls to ever-raging demon gods'<br /> <br /> <b>52. Is there any threat big enough that we could work together with Lunars to stop it? How big? How many Lunars?</b><br /> <br /> If we discover a wacky negaverse-Creation with even MORE Lunars, I will extend the hand of truce in order to stop those.<br /> <br /> <b>53. Does creating or encouraging schools of thaumaturgy, Terrestrial Martial Arts, or Sorcery among mortals threaten fate, or could it be a tool to help humans or oppose enemies of Creation? If so how should we go about doing that?</b><br /> <br /> Are you trying to get placed as Director of Educational Outreach or something? Because we outsourced that to Malfeas seven hundred years ago.<br /> <br /> <b>54. How much occult knowledge should mortals have? How much is enough to know how to avoid the most common demon/fae/ghost tricks, demon escapes, etc.? How much is too much (enough to start doing dangerous shit)?</b><br /> <br /> They also probably shouldn't be trusted with the <i>Word Which Causes Instant Death If You Know It.</i><br /> <br /> <b>55. (Bronze) Should we try to pry the Emerald Thurible out of Mnemon's hands?</b><br /> <br /> No. I saw her lick it.<br /> <br /> <b>56. How much time and effort and money should we spend trying to stamp out necromancy and hungry ghost creation among mortals?</b><br /> <br /> I have really awful news about how the last part of this solution would have to go.<br /> <br /> <b>57. How much time and effort and money should we spend trying to stamp out ancestor worship among mortals?</b><br /> <br /> Already done- I've cleverly murdered all the ancestors.<br /> <br /> <b>58. Can we use the Mountain Folk more... usefully? They don't exactly have mountains of starmetal but they can do and make cool stuff.</b><br /> <br /> It's really dark down there and I think I saw a spider.<br /> <br /> <b>59. Bureau of Humanity vs. Bureau of Destiny dispute who has more jurisdiction over warfare. How important is this?</b><br /> <br /> Oh my god Mars shut up shut up shut up I don't CARE what Ahlat said about the proper state of mind for second talonlords! If they want to be in charge of war so much just LET THEM!<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T23:18:18-07:00","id":685320,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Maiden Mercury, I believe you've a just created a 'meme.' Far be it from me to question your judgement. Shall I begin the appropriate prayers and offerings entreating the pattern spiders to start tweeting #JohnCenaForScarletEmpress? Also, on a note of purely personal curiosity, is John Stewart one of your guises? </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T05:13:56-07:00","id":685525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=684962#post684962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matron.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree. In general, I'd like more focus on religion and philosophy in Creation. The Sidereals are particularly interesting, as their gods are actually literally their bosses.</div> </div> </div> </div>An excellent point, and I can see why you'd say that. I thought about using that that way, but I wasn't sure it held the same connotation, so I didn't. I'd change it, but that would make your answer somewhat more confusing to those newcomers who come visit this topic. That said, I totally want to see more philosophy, religion, and cultic practice in Creation. There's such potential for interesting depth to be added to the setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=684986#post684986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually the scriptures were <b>adopted</b> by the individual Maidens according to preference - Sidereals 1e made it clear that someone left them entangled into the Loom itself from where they were taken by the Maidens for their own reasons and made charms from. If it was Jupiter or someone else altogether that left the scriptures there in the first place is in itself pretty much a mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the more reason to discuss them in depth! Who knows what mysteries might stand revealed? There's such potential for knowledge, one that I feel many Sidereals would find difficult to resist - especially Chosen of Jupiter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T05:41:50-07:00","id":685574,"title":"","content":"One thing that occurred to me recently is the Bronze Faction has much less reason to invest so heavily in the Realm as it did in past editions. In 1E/2E, the Thousand Dooms gave Kejak and Co. plenty of good reasons to back a ruthless, powerful single actor to control most of Creation. When we lessen those threats, there is much less reason to insist that the Realm is the only horse worth backing.<br /> <br /> So, I can imagine that the Bronze faction debated cultivating other options. Some would want to support Lookshy more surely. Some would want to try spreading the blood of the Dragons wider amongst Creation. Some could more easily take issue with the atrocities of the Realm, and argue for withdrawing support. I can even see some of the Bronzies arguing for attempting contact with the Lunars, and offering to help them build kingdoms on the border of Creation, to keep out the fae.<br /> <br /> When Creation was under constant threat of being destroyed, it made sense for Kejak to humble himself and play along with Scarlet. Without that constant threat, it makes more sense to cultivate multiple negotiation partners, if for no other reason than to remind Her Redness she is not the only game in town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T06:11:16-07:00","id":685606,"title":"","content":"60.) When should we recall and debrief the Green Lady?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T06:19:32-07:00","id":685623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=685606#post685606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">60.) When should we recall and debrief the Green Lady?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals have developed the powerful Scarlet Eruptions of Perversion Style as a defensive measure against having their briefs stolen. Be assured that whoever invoked the Green Lady's ire in this fashion would fall victim to the dreaded Thousand Pints Jet Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T06:57:26-07:00","id":685676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=685606#post685606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">60.) When should we recall and debrief the Green Lady?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to debrief the Green Lady at any time. *eyebrow waggle*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:46:04-07:00","id":685859,"title":"","content":"I know you started with &quot;most of the Sidereals aren't old enough to remember the Prophesy&quot;, but a goodly percent of them <i>are</i> old enough to have been personally present during many of Creation's more recent pivotal historical moments. I think it's interesting to think about what opinion people like Anys Syn <i>had</i> on, for instance, the rise of the Empress, back when it was happening, or what Sad Ivory might have been doing during the Gunzota Incident, or what sorts of Heavenly political intrigue may have accompanied the founding of the Confederation of Rivers.<br /> <br /> Also, it's important to remember that &quot;Do you support the returning Solars Y/N&quot; has only been the divisive Gold/Bronze question for the last couple years. Before that it was more &quot;Are you still pissed off about the Usurpation Y/N&quot;. To your point, most of the Sidereals aren't nearly old enough to have any real sense of remember when it was &quot;Should we try to reform the Solars Y/N&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T10:02:08-07:00","id":685874,"title":"","content":"That's only because the Gold Faction are depicted as doing nothing at all during the Age of Sorrows other than bemoaning the world falling apart. They could have started right away trying to find Solars, figure out why they go crazy and how to prevent it, and planned out how to find and break the Jade Prison. Even if Ayesha Ura was content to sit on her bum twiddling her thumbs and complaining for 700 years, surely some other Goldies would have advocated actually doing something constructive, if they honestly believed it was necessary to protect Creation. Those guys would surely have debated what to do, instead of giving up.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the Bronzies would have been debating the founding of the Empire, how it should be done and how to &quot;handle&quot; the Empress who didn't really want to be handled, and what to do with Lookshy, etc.<br /> <br /> Surely everybody had an opinion on &quot;Should we continue to kill entirely new Solars/Lunars or are new ones not a threat to Creation?&quot; which continued to be relevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway. Back to OP topic.<br /> <br /> Then the Guild starts up an everyone probably has an opinion about that. I think that could be pretty interesting. They essentially became a major power with real pull in the world -- not like the Empire, but enough to seriously affect things, and run entirely by mortals.<br /> <br /> What was the Gunzota Incident?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T10:31:40-07:00","id":685909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=685874#post685874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's only because the Gold Faction are depicted as doing nothing at all during the Age of Sorrows other than bemoaning the world falling apart.They could have started right away trying to find Solars, figure out why they go crazy and how to prevent it, and planned out how to find and break the Jade Prison.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's confirmed that they did at least some of that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP:Sidereals page 27</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Most of all, the Gold Faction sought the Jade Prison\u2019s location in hopes the faction could liberate the Solar Exaltations. Neither sorcery nor the Loom of Fate could find it, though, so the Gold Faction Sidereals looked outside fate, in the Wyld... and the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:14:06-07:00","id":686102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=685859#post685859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you started with &quot;most of the Sidereals aren't old enough to remember the Prophesy&quot;, but a goodly percent of them <i>are</i> old enough to have been personally present during many of Creation's more recent pivotal historical moments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. Probably not. <br /> <br /> I'd bet most current Sidereals are less than a couple centuries old.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of turnover when going into Creation basically means being Muldoon hunting raptors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T17:31:34-07:00","id":686298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=686102#post686102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. Probably not.<br /> <br /> I'd bet most current Sidereals are less than a couple centuries old.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of turnover when going into Creation basically means being Muldoon hunting raptors.</div> </div> </div> </div>True - the fact Sidereals have a potential lifespan of millenia doesn't mean most of them have millenia of existence any more than for Lunars or any other hypothetical &quot;stealth celestial&quot; that might be or have been around in the centuries since the Usurpation....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-02-2015, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T03:30:15-07:00","id":686738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=686102#post686102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. Probably not.<br /> <br /> I'd bet most current Sidereals are less than a couple centuries old.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of turnover when going into Creation basically means being Muldoon hunting raptors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Sidereals on the field do not, on average, live long and productive lives. Sidereals are basically the MI5 agents - their missions tend to involve some seriously outrageous shit with some very real chance of biting it. And when you spend your life in missions with risk of death, sooner or later the dice come up snake eyes.<br /> <br /> Sometimes literally, seeing how Lunars are a thing :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T12:10:56-07:00","id":691543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/684528-hot-button-political-issues-for-sidereals?p=686738#post686738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much. Sidereals on the field do not, on average, live long and productive lives. Sidereals are basically the MI5 agents - their missions tend to involve some seriously outrageous shit with some very real chance of biting it. And when you spend your life in missions with risk of death, sooner or later the dice come up snake eyes.<br /> <br /> Sometimes literally, seeing how Lunars are a thing :P.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, it's sort of telling of this the fact that at least two chairpeople of the directional conventions (Ayesha Ura and Nazri) are post-Usurpation sidereals and a third (Righteous Tsunami) is post-Contagion.<br /> <br /> And the Convention of Air has been leaderless since the events of the Tepet's campaign against the Bull of the North - it's situation is so bad at present even a well-motivated clique of young sidereal PCs might have a decent chance of getting a new convention head in the chair. Hmmmm, i think i now know just the perfect way to mess with my Sids group when i return to that game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-06-2015, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}